{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-08-07T18:44:30, and the GPS trace then places the driver inside the LARGE_VENUE arrival radius of 120 m from 18:44:45, generating 40 qualifying in-radius fixes across two separate holds (18:44:45-18:47:35 and 18:49:35-18:52:40). That is far more than the three consecutive in-radius fixes POL-NS-02 requires before arrival is deemed established, so POL-NS-01 limb (a) and the POL-NS-02 proximity test are both satisfied on the trace's own numbers.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00214", "EV-GPS-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no false arrival marker to attack. Nothing in the record places the driver more than 300 m from the pin or moving at 15 km/h or above at the 18:44:30 marker: the derived excursion block measures the driver's furthest point between the two holds at 178.95 m, and it records the POL-NS-06(i) limb as available rather than flagging any false-arrival condition. Even on the rider's best case that the marker preceded the first in-radius fix by a single 10 second sampling interval, POL-NS-05(iii) applies: the waiting clock is recomputed to the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 18:44:45, and because the corrected dwell still exceeds the 300 second minimum the false marker does not by itself defeat the fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00214", "EV-TRIP-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.max_excursion_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The effective in-geofence dwell is 355 accumulated seconds - two holds of 170 s and 185 s - against the LARGE_VENUE minimum of 300 s. The derived shortfall is minus 55 seconds, meaning there is no shortfall at all, so POL-NS-06 returns no refund. The rider's assertion that the driver 'never even stayed 5 minutes in one place' misdescribes the test: the required dwell need not be served in one place, because POL-NS-06(i) expressly permits separate in-geofence intervals within a single pickup attempt to be summed toward the 300 second minimum.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.accumulated_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) is available on this record because EV-ADVIS-00214-01 is present and populated with type KERB_RESTRICTION: an LTA DataMall full-day bus lane on Orchard Road and Orchard Turn in force 17:00-20:00, with TrafficMarshals and enforcement cameras active, whose geometry covers the pickup road and whose active window covers the whole 18:38-18:52 trip window. The limb's distance qualification is met too - the driver's furthest point between the intervals was 178.95 m, inside the 300 m leash. The trace's larger whole-run maximum of 1191.8 m is not a position inside either in-geofence hold (a hold is by definition within 120 m of the pin) but a start-of-trace approach figure, the trace opening at 18:39:05, five minutes before the 18:44:30 arrival.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00214-01", "EV-GPS-00214", "EV-TRIP-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.max_excursion_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own chat account of why he moved - that the marshal made him move because the bus lane runs until 8pm, and that he told the rider he was going one round and coming back to the same place - is corroborated by the LTA advisory for exactly that road and window, and the trace matches it fix for fix: he leaves the geofence at 18:47:35 and is back inside it at 18:49:35, a 120 second loop whose furthest point is 178.95 m from the pin, followed by a further 185 second hold. That is a driver complying with a no-stopping kerb, which is the very situation POL-NS-06(i) was drafted to cover, not a driver abandoning the pickup.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00214", "EV-ADVIS-00214-01", "EV-GPS-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.runs",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-01 limb (d) is satisfied on the trip record's own fields: the trip was terminated by the driver at 18:52:45 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, five seconds after the last qualifying in-geofence fix at 18:52:40, and there is no boarding event anywhere in the record - started_at and ended_at are both null. RIDER_NO_SHOW is one of the three reason codes the limb recognises, and the recorded wait_time_min of 8.3 minutes is consistent with the 18:44:30 arrival marker and the 18:52:45 cancellation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00214", "EV-GPS-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own track places her device between 690.7 m and 717.2 m from the pickup pin across all 70 fixes in the waiting window, at zero speed throughout, and the qualifying rider fix count against the 150 m LARGE_VENUE presence radius is nil. She was not at the pickup and not approaching it at any moment before cancellation. That answers 'I was coming down for you' and removes limb (c) of POL-NS-04 from the case: the rider-exoneration route cannot be run on this trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00214", "EV-CHAT-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Independently of presence, POL-NS-04 does not apply because the driver answered inside the 120 second window: the rider's 'ok coming down now' was sent at 18:46:20 and the driver's reply - that the marshal had moved him and he was going one round and returning to the same place - was sent at 18:47:50, 90 seconds later. Limb (b) therefore fails, and any residual coordination question is decided under POL-NS-01 and POL-NS-06 rather than by exonerating the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00214", "EV-TRIP-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-03 has no purchase on these facts. That clause governs a driver stationary for the required dwell outside the POL-NS-02 arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin; here the driver's two stationary holds are inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius at a pickup with a single registered point (venue_id VEN-ION-ORCHARD, registered_pickup_points 1), so no wrong-entrance, wrong-block or pin-ambiguity case arises and no goodwill payment is in issue.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00214", "EV-TRIP-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "With POL-NS-01 satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displacing it, the driver is compensated at 80 per cent of the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee, that is SGD 3.20, under POL-NS-07. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below the threshold of 4, and 2 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 118 is 0.017, below the threshold of 0.08. The clause requires both limbs and neither is met, so compensation is payable rather than withheld.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00214", "EV-DPROF-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The SGD 4.00 actually charged reconciles under POL-NS-08(d): it is the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee of SGD 4.00 and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee of SGD 4.00, the two dimensions agreeing, so there is no fare defect and no basis for splitting the fee. The ledger shows payment_status CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so on this rider-filed dispute the correct disposition of the contested amount is that the present charge stands, with the SGD 3.20 driver payment recorded as an independent, platform-funded figure per POL-GEN-03 and never netted against the rider's fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00214", "EV-TRIP-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is engaged, so this case is decidable on the record and the fee should not be placed on hold. The two admissible traces agree rather than contradict (arrival 18:44:30, cancellation 18:52:45, 8.3 minutes); every one of the seven artifacts in the bundle is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so no deciding fact rests on impaired evidence; the parties share no other no-show dispute in the trailing 90 days, both disputes_with_counterparty_90d being 0; the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip; and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the threshold of 3.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00214", "EV-GPS-00214", "EV-DPROF-00214", "EV-RPROF-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.2,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.2,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both parties' accounts and the platform telemetry line up on the material facts. The driver marked arrival at 18:44:30, held at the ION PHV bay for 170 seconds (18:44:45 to 18:47:35), was moved off the kerb by the marshal because the Orchard Road bus lane was in force until 20:00, drove a 120-second loop that took him no further than 178.95 m from the pin, re-entered the bay at 18:49:35 and held a further 185 seconds until 18:52:40, then cancelled at 18:52:45 recording RIDER_NO_SHOW. Nothing was boarded (started_at and ended_at are null).\n\nTo the rider: (1) You say he never stayed five minutes in one place. The 300-second minimum for a LARGE_VENUE pickup need not be served continuously in one spot: POL-NS-06(i) lets separate in-geofence intervals be summed where an LTA advisory covers the pickup road and the driver never went more than 300 m from the pin. EV-ADVIS-00214-01 is a populated KERB_RESTRICTION (full-day bus lane, Orchard Road/Orchard Turn, 17:00 to 20:00, marshals and cameras active) covering the whole trip window, and the driver's furthest point between the two holds was 178.95 m, inside the 300 m leash. The summed dwell is 355 seconds, 55 seconds above the 300-second minimum, so POL-NS-06 produces no shortfall and no refund. (2) You point to the trace's 1,191.8 m maximum distance. That figure is from the driver's approach before he reached the bay (the trace opens at 18:39:05, roughly five minutes before arrival), not from the leaving-and-re-entering the leash governs; inside the pickup attempt the maximum is 178.95 m. (3) You note the first in-geofence fix (18:44:45) is 15 seconds after the 18:44:30 marker. POL-NS-02 makes limb (b) fail only where the trace contains no qualifying in-radius fix in the 15 minutes before cancellation; there are 40 qualifying in-radius fixes here, so arrival is established, and any marker imprecision is handled by POL-NS-05(iii) - the clock runs from the first qualifying fix and the corrected dwell still exceeds the minimum. (4) The 8.3-minute wait_time_min is elapsed time from the marker to cancellation, not dwell; the dwell measured from the trace is 355 seconds. POL-NS-04 does not assist you either: the driver replied 90 seconds after your 18:46:20 message, inside the 120-second window, so that clause does not run.\n\nTo the driver: your arrival is established on the 40 qualifying in-radius fixes, the KERB_RESTRICTION advisory supports accumulating your two holds, and limb (d) is satisfied (you terminated the trip with RIDER_NO_SHOW and no boarding event is recorded). The anti-farming check does not trip - no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below 4) and 2 divided by 118 completed trips is 0.017 (below 0.08) - so compensation is payable rather than withheld.\n\nThe amount: the contested charge of SGD 4.00 stands. It reconciles with the greater of the SGD 4.00 LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee, so there is no fare defect under POL-NS-08(d). Under POL-NS-07 you are compensated at 80 per cent of that fee, SGD 3.20 of SGD 4.00, funded by the platform and not netted against the rider's charge. No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is engaged (all seven artifacts are complete at weight 1.0, the traces agree, and neither party has another no-show dispute with the other in the trailing 90 days), so nothing is held and no referral is produced. The rider's claim is not supported on the evidence and the present charge stands."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
